  "stem": "The angular frequency of the damped oscillator is given by ω = $\\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m} - \\frac{r^{2}}{4m^{2}}}\\ $where k is the spring constant, m is the mass of the oscillator and r is the damping constant. If the ratio $\\frac{r^{2}}{mk}$ is 8%, the change in time period compared to the undamped oscillator is approximately:",
  "options": {
    "A": "Decreases by 1%",
    "B": "Increases by 8%",
    "C": "Increases by 1%",
    "D": "Decreases by 8%"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "C"
    ]
  },
